## Experimental Parameters

The targeted fingerprinting framework was designed to evaluate how different client-side configurations influence Tor Browser traffic patterns. Parameters were varied independently to isolate their effect on encrypted network traces.

### 1. Browser Versions

To evaluate robustness across software updates, experiments were conducted using multiple Tor Browser releases:

| Browser Version     | Purpose                   |
| ------------------- | ------------------------- |
| Tor Browser 13.0.15 | Baseline stable release   |
| Tor Browser 13.0.16 | Minor update comparison   |
| Tor Browser 13.5a8  | Alpha release evaluation  |
| Tor Browser 13.5.9a | New alpha release testing |

Browser versions were selected based on significant changes to rendering behaviour, networking components, and privacy mechanisms.

---

