## Experimental Design

To maintain scientific validity, only one parameter was varied at a time while all other settings remained fixed. This parameter isolation strategy ensured that any observed differences in network traffic could be attributed directly to the configuration under investigation.

The resulting datasets were used to evaluate both:

1. Traditional Website Fingerprinting (Website Classification)
2. Targeted Configuration Fingerprinting (Client Configuration Classification)

This methodology enabled systematic analysis of how browser settings, operating systems, network environments, and software versions contribute to traffic fingerprinting attacks against Tor users.
